// spring_damper(hertz: float, damping_ratio: float, position: float, velocity:
//   float, time_step: float) -> float
// One-dimensional mass-spring-damper simulation. Returns the new velocity given
// the position and time step. You can then compute the new position using:
// position += timeStep * newVelocity This drives towards a zero position. By
// using implicit integration we get a stable solution that doesn't require
// transcendental functions.
// C: `float b2SpringDamper(float hertz, float dampingRatio, float position,
// float velocity, float timeStep)`
